Package: predpower
Title: Design-Stage Assessment of Out-of-Sample Prediction Accuracy
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Elizabeth", "Tipton", email = "tipton@northwestern.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: Power-analysis-style calculations for prediction studies. Given a
    sample size, a number of predictors, an assumed in-sample signal and a
    design efficiency factor, returns the expected out-of-sample R-squared and
    the expected correlation between observed and predicted outcomes, under
    ordinary least squares and under ridge regression at the design-implied
    penalty. Computes the design efficiency factor from a covariate matrix,
    supplies confidence intervals for the assumed signal by inverting the
    noncentral F or, when there are more predictors than observations, by
    restricted maximum likelihood under the ridge prior, and solves for the sample size, signal, number of predictors
    or design efficiency a study would need to beat the sample mean. All
    quantities are computable before any outcome is observed.
